itors store charge and electrostatic energy.", "tags": [ "electronics" ], "status": "active" }, { "id": "ELX-000010", "category": "Electronics", "subcategory": "Digital", "difficulty": "medium", "question": "Which digital logic gate produces a LOW (0) output only when both inputs are HIGH (1)?", "options": [ "NAND Gate", "NOR Gate", "AND Gate", "XOR Gate" ], "answer": 0, "explanation": "NAND gate is the inverse of an AND gate.", "tags": [ "electronics" ], "status": "active" }, { "id": "ELX-000011", "category": "Electronics", "subcategory": "Oscillators", "difficulty": "hard", "question": "What type of multivibrator circuit has no stable states and continuously oscillates generating a square wave?", "options": [ "Astable Multivibrator", "Monostable Multivibrator", "Bistable Flip-Flop", "Schmitt Trigger" ], "answer": 0, "explanation": "Astable multivibrators oscillate freely without external triggers.", "tags": [ "electronics" ], "status": "active" }, { "id": "ELX-000012", "category": "Electronics", "subcategory": "Diodes", "difficulty": "easy", "question": "What type of diode is designed to operate reliably in its reverse breakdown region to regulate voltage?", "options": [ "Zener Diode", "Schottky Diode", "Varactor Diode", "Tunnel Diode" ], "answer": 0, "explanation": "Zener diodes maintain a constant reverse breakdown reference voltage.", "tags": [ "electronics" ], "status": "active" }, { "id": "ELX-000013", "category": "Electronics", "subcategory": "Filtering", "difficulty": "medium", "question": "What passive filter circuit configuration allows high frequencies to pass while attenuating low frequencies?", "options": [ "High-Pass Filter (Series capacitor with shunt resistor)", "Low-Pass Filter", "Band-Stop Filter", "Notch Filter" ], "answer": 0, "explanation": "A High-Pass Filter blocks DC and low frequencies.", "tags": [ "electronics" ], "status": "active" }, { "id": "ELX-000014", "category": "Electronics", "subcategory": "Feedback", "difficulty": "hard", "questi