ive naval battle in 1805 established British naval supremacy during the Napoleonic Wars?", "options": [ "Battle of Trafalgar", "Battle of Waterloo", "Battle of Jutland", "Battle of the Nile" ], "answer": 0, "explanation": "Admiral Lord Nelson defeated the Franco-Spanish fleet at Trafalgar in 1805.", "tags": [ "history" ], "status": "active" }, { "id": "HVAC-000001", "category": "HVAC", "subcategory": "Airflow", "difficulty": "easy", "question": "What standard unit measures volumetric airflow rate in HVAC ductwork?", "options": [ "CFM (Cubic Feet per Minute)", "PSI", "BTU", "RPM" ], "answer": 0, "explanation": "CFM measures cubic feet of air moved per minute.", "tags": [ "hvac" ], "status": "active" }, { "id": "HVAC-000002", "category": "HVAC", "subcategory": "Capacity", "difficulty": "easy", "question": "How many BTUs per hour equal 1 standard ton of refrigeration?", "options": [ "12,000 BTU/hr", "24,000 BTU/hr", "6,000 BTU/hr", "100,000 BTU/hr" ], "answer": 0, "explanation": "1 ton of refrigeration = 12,000 BTU/hr.", "tags": [ "hvac" ], "status": "active" }, { "id": "HVAC-000003", "category": "HVAC", "subcategory": "Filters", "difficulty": "easy", "question": "What does a filter's MERV rating indicate?", "options": [ "Minimum Efficiency Reporting Value", "Motor Energy Resistance", "Moisture Evaporation", "Mass Energy Radiation" ], "answer": 0, "explanation": "MERV measures particle filtration efficiency.", "tags": [ "hvac" ], "status": "active" }, { "id": "HVAC-000004", "category": "HVAC", "subcategory": "Thermostats", "difficulty": "easy", "question": "In standard thermostat wiring, which color wire typically signals cooling?", "options": [ "Yellow (Y)", "Red (R)", "White (W)", "Green (G)" ], "answer": 0, "explanation": "Yellow (Y) controls the cooling compressor contactor.", "tags": [ "hvac" ], "status": "active" }, { "id": "HVAC-000005", "category": "HVAC", "subcategory": "Safety", "difficulty": "easy", "question": "What toxic gas can be produced by a cracked furnace heat exchanger?", "options": [ "Carbon Monoxide (CO)", "Carbon Dioxide", "Nitrogen", "Argon" ], "answer": 0, "explanation": "Incomplete combustion yields Carbon Monoxide.", "tags": [ "hvac" ], "status": "active" }, { "id": "HVAC-000006", "category": "HVAC", "subcategory": "Components", "difficulty": "easy", "question": "Which component circulates and compresses refrigerant gas throughout the cycle?", "options": [ "Compressor", "Evaporator", "Condenser fan", "Filter drier" ], "answer": 0, "explanation": "The compressor raises refrigerant pressure and temperature.", "tags": [ "hvac" ], "status": "active" }, { "id": "HVAC-000007", "category": "HVAC", "subcategory": "Refrigeration", "difficulty": "medium", "question": "What is the primary function of the expansion valve (TXV)?", "options": [ "Drop refrigerant pressure and temperature entering the evaporator", "Compress vapor", "Condense hot gas", "Filter oil" ], "answer": 0, "explanation": "The TXV meters refrigerant and lowers its pressure.", "tags": [ "hvac" ], "status": "active" }, { "id": "HVAC-000008", "category": "HVAC", "subcategory": "Refrigerants", "difficulty": "medium", "question": "Why is R-410A considered near-azeotropic?", "options": [ "It has near-zero temperature glide during phase change", "It contains chlorine", "It operates at low pressure", "It can be vented directly" ], "answer": 0, "explanation": "R-410A behaves almost like a single-compound fluid.", "tags": [ "hvac" ], "status": "active" }, { "id": "HVAC-000009", "category": "HVAC", "subcategory": "Psychrometrics", "difficulty": "medium", "question": "What is the relative humidity when dry-bulb equals wet-bulb temperature?", "options": [ "100% Relative Humidity", "0%", "50%", "75%" ], "answer": 0, "explanation": "Equal dry and wet bulb temperatures mean 100% RH saturation.", "tags": [ "hvac" ], "status": "active" }, { "id": "HVAC-000010", "category": "HVAC", "subcategory": "Motors", "difficulty": "medium", "question": "Which blower motor modulates speed to maintain constant airflow against static pressure?", "options": [ "ECM (Electronically Commutated Motor)", "PSC Motor", "Shaded Pole", "Split Phase" ], "answer": 0, "explanation": "ECM motors modulate speed to maintain target CFM.", "tags": [ "hvac" ], "status": "active" }, { "id": "HVAC-000011", "category": "HVAC", "subcategory": "Superheat", "difficulty": "medium", "question": "How is total superheat calculated on an operating AC system?", "options": [ "Suction line temperature minus evaporator saturation temperature", "Liquid line temp minus condenser temp", "Discharge temp minus suction temp", "Outdoor temp minus indoor temp" ], "answer": 0, "explanation": "Superheat = Suction Line Temp - Evaporator Saturation Temp.", "tags": [ "hvac" ], "status": "active" }, { "id": "HVAC-000012", "category": "HVAC", "subcategory": "Subcooling", "difficulty": "medium", "question": "How is total subcooling calculated on an air conditioning condenser?", "options": [ "Condenser saturation temperature minus liquid line temperature", "Suction temp minus liquid temp", "Outdoor temp plus indoor temp", "Discharge pressure divided by 2" ], "answer": 0, "explanation": "Subcooling = Condenser Saturation Temp - Liquid Line Temp.", "tags": [ "hvac" ], "status": "active" }, { "id": "HVAC-000013", "category": "HVAC", "subcategory": "Thermodynamics", "difficulty": "hard", "question": "What is heat that causes temperature change without changing state of matter?", "options": [ "Sensible Heat", "Latent Heat", "Specific Heat Ratio", "Subcooling Enthalpy" ], "answer": 0, "explanation": "Sensible heat causes a measurable temperature change.", "tags": [ "hvac" ], "status": "active" }, { "id": "HVAC-000014", "category": "HVAC", "subcategory": "Diagnostics", "difficulty": "hard", "question": "In a TXV system, high superheat combined with low subcooling indicates what?", "options": [ "Undercharged system (low refrigerant)", "Overcharged system", "Liquid line restriction", "Dirty air filter" ], "answer": 0, "explanation": "An undercharged system shows high superheat and low subcooling.", "tags": [ "hvac" ], "status": "active" }, { "id": "HVAC-000015", "category": "HVAC", "subcategory": "Evacuation", "difficulty": "hard", "question": "What vacuum level in microns must be achieved for system deep dehydration?", "options": [ "500 microns or lower", "5,000 microns", "29.9 inches Hg", "15,000 microns" ], "answer": 0, "explanation": "500 microns ensures complete moisture evaporation.", "tags": [ "hvac" ], "status": "active" }, { "id": "HVAC-000016", "category": "HVAC", "subcategory": "Reversing Valves", "difficulty": "hard", "question": "In a heat pump reversing valve, what mechanism shifts the internal sliding valve spool?", "options": [ "Pressure differential between high and low side routed by a pilot solenoid", "Direct mechanical gear motor", "Bimetallic expansion spring", "Centrifugal air fan" ], "answer": 0, "explanation": "Reversing valves use pilot solenoids to create a pressure differential.", "tags": [ "hvac" ], "status": "active" }, { "id": "HVAC-000017", "category": "HVAC", "subcategory": "Safety", "difficulty": "easy", "question": "What device shuts off power to a gas furnace if flames roll out of the combustion chamber?", "options": [ "Flame Rollout Switch", "Blower door switch", "Thermostat", "Contactor" ], "answer": 0, "explanation": "The flame rollout thermal limit switch trips if flames spill outward.", "tags": [ "hvac" ], "status": "active" }, { "id": "HVAC-000018", "category": "HVAC", "subcategory": "Air Quality", "difficulty": "medium", "question": "What is the primary function of an Economizer in commercial rooftop HVAC units?", "options": [ "Use cool outdoor ambient air for free cooling when conditions are favorable", "Heat intake air with gas", "Filter ultra-fine carbon soot", "Compress liquid refrigerant" ], "answer": 0, "explanation": "Economizers draw in cool outside air to reduce compressor run-time.", "tags": [ "hvac" ], "status": "active" }, { "id": "HVAC-000019", "category": "HVAC", "subcategory": "Psychrometrics", "difficulty": "hard", "question": "On a psychrometric chart, what property remains constant along horizontal straight lines?", "options": [ "Humidity Ratio (Specific Humidity / Dew Point)", "Dry-Bulb Temperature", "Enthalpy", "Relative Humidity" ], "answer": 0, "explanation": "Horizontal lines represent constant moisture content and dew point.", "tags": [ "hvac" ], "status": "active" }, { "id": "HVAC-000020", "category": "HVAC", "subcategory": "Piping", "difficulty": "easy", "question": "What type of copper tubing is most commonly used in air conditioning refrigeration lines?", "options": [ "ACR Copper (dehydrated and sealed)", "Type M Plumbing Copper", "PVC Pipe", "Cast Iron" ], "answer": 0, "explanation": "ACR copper is cleaned, dehydrated, and nitrogen-pressurized.", "tags": [ "hvac" ], "status": "active" }, { "id": "HVAC-000021", "category": "HVAC", "subcategory": "Combustion", "difficulty": "medium", "question": "What is the theoretical perfect combustion air-to-natural-gas volume ratio?", "options": [ "Approx 10 parts air to 1 part natural gas (10:1)", "2:1", "50:1", "100:1" ], "answer": 0, "explanation": "Natural gas requires roughly 10 cubic feet of air per 1 cubic foot of gas for complete combustion.", "tags": [ "hvac" ], "status": "active" }, { "id": "HVAC-000022", "category": "HVAC", "subcategory": "Compressors", "difficulty": "hard", "question": "In a scroll compressor, what motion does the orbiting scroll make relative to the stationary scroll?", "options": [ "Orbital circular oscillation without rotating", "Linear reciprocating stroke", "Rotary vane spin at 3600 RPM", "Screw axial rotation" ], "answer": 0, "explanation": "The orbiting scroll oscillates in an eccentric circular orbit without rotating.", "tags": [ "hvac" ], "status": "active" }, { "id": "HVAC-EASY-001-1", "category": "HVAC", "subcategory": "HVAC", "difficulty": "easy", "question": "Which term is best described by the following definition: a thermodynamic cycle used to transfer heat from a lower-temperature region to a higher-temperature sink?", "options": [ "SEER", "Refrigeration cycle", "CFM", "Expansion device" ], "answer": 1, "explanation": "The correct answer is Refrigeration cycle. It matches the defining characteristic or role described in the question.", "tags": [ "hvac" ], "status": "active" }, { "id": "HVAC-MEDIUM-001-2", "category": "HVAC", "subcategory": "HVAC", "difficulty": "medium", "question": "Which statement best describes Refrigeration cycle?", "options": [ "the temperature at which a substance changes phase at a specified pressure", "a control or system that uses favorable outdoor conditions to reduce mechanical cooling", "temperature of vapor above its saturation temperature at a given pressure", "a thermodynamic cycle used to transfer heat from a lower-temperature region to a higher-temperature sink" ], "answer": 3, "explanation": "The correct answer is a thermodynamic cycle used to transfer heat from a lower-temperature region to a higher-temperature sink. It matches the defining characteristic or role described in the question.", "tags": [ "hvac" ], "status": "active" }, { "id": "HVAC-HARD-001-3", "category": "HVAC", "subcategory": "HVAC", "difficulty": "hard", "question": "A learner encounters this situation: a system removes heat from a conditioned space and rejects it outdoors. Which concept best matches it?", "options": [ "VAV", "Refrigeration cycle", "Subcooling", "EER" ], "answer": 1, "explanation": "The correct answer is Refrigeration cycle. It matches the defining characteristic or role described in the question.", "tags": [ "hvac" ], "status": "active" }, { "id": "HVAC-EASY-001-4", "category": "HVAC", "subcategory": "HVAC", "difficulty": "easy", "question": "Which option best identifies the primary purpose or role associated with Refrigeration cycle?", "options": [ "provide cooling by moving heat", "transport air", "create a