ed by the following definition: a working fluid that absorbs and rejects heat through phase and temperature changes?", "options": [ "Evaporator", "Refrigerant", "Condenser", "Subcooling" ], "answer": 1, "explanation": "The correct answer is Refrigerant. It matches the defining characteristic or role described in the question.", "tags": [ "hvac" ], "status": "active" }, { "id": "HVAC-MEDIUM-022-2", "category": "HVAC", "subcategory": "HVAC", "difficulty": "medium", "question": "Which statement best describes Refrigerant?", "options": [ "Energy Efficiency Ratio, a ratio of cooling capacity to electrical input under specified conditions", "a thermodynamic cycle used to transfer heat from a lower-temperature region to a higher-temperature sink", "temperature of vapor above its saturation temperature at a given pressure", "a working fluid that absorbs and rejects heat through phase and temperature changes" ], "answer": 3, "explanation": "The correct answer is a working fluid that absorbs and rejects heat through phase and temperature changes. It matches the defining characteristic or role described in the question.", "tags": [ "hvac" ], "status": "active" }, { "id": "HVAC-HARD-022-3", "category": "HVAC", "subcategory": "HVAC", "difficulty": "hard", "question": "A learner encounters this situation: a vapor-compression system circulates a specialized fluid. Which concept best matches it?", "options": [ "Psychrometrics", "Ductwork", "Refrigerant", "Thermostat" ], "answer": 2, "explanation": "The correct answer is Refrigerant. It matches the defining characteristic or role described in the question.", "tags": [ "hvac" ], "status": "active" }, { "id": "HVAC-EASY-022-4", "category": "HVAC", "subcategory": "HVAC", "difficulty": "easy", "question": "Which option best identifies the primary purpose or role associated with Refrigerant?", "options": [ "reduce airborne particulate matter", "express heat quantity in traditional HVAC terms", "absorb heat from the conditioned space", "transfer heat through the refrigeration cycle" ], "answer": 3, "explanation": "The correct answer is transfer heat through the refrigeration cycle. It matches the defining characteristic or role described in the question.", "tags": [ "hvac" ], "status": "active" }, { "id": "HVAC-EASY-023-1", "category": "HVAC", "subcategory": "HVAC", "difficulty": "easy", "question": "Which term is best described by the following definition: a network of passages used to distribute conditioned air?", "options": [ "Superheat", "BTU", "Ductwork", "Static pressure" ], "answer": 2, "explanation": "The correct answer is Ductwork. It matches the defining characteristic or role described in the question.", "tags": [ "hvac" ], "status": "active" }, { "id": "HVAC-MEDIUM-023-2", "category": "HVAC", "subcategory": "HVAC", "difficulty": "medium", "question": "Which statement best describes Ductwork?", "options": [ "a heat exchanger where high-pressure refrigerant vapor rejects heat and condenses", "a control or system that uses favorable outdoor conditions to reduce mechanical cooling", "a thermodynamic cycle used to transfer heat from a lower-temperature region to a higher-temperature sink", "a network of passages used to distribute conditioned air" ], "answer": 3, "explanation": "The correct answer is a network of passages used to distribute conditioned air. It matches the defining characteristic or role described in the question.", "tags": [ "hvac" ], "status": "active" }, { "id": "HVAC-HARD-023-3", "category": "HVAC", "subcategory": "HVAC", "difficulty": "hard", "question": "A learner encounters this situation: supply and return ducts carry air through a building. Which concept best matches it?", "options": [ "Static pressure", "Air filter", "Ductwork", "Heat pump" ], "answer": 2, "explanation": "The correct answer is Ductwork. It matches the defining characteristic or role described in the question.", "tags": [ "hvac" ], "status": "active" }, { "id": "HVAC-MEDIUM-023-4", "category": "HVAC", "subcategory": "HVAC", "difficulty": "medium", "question": "Which option best identifies the primary purpose or role associated with Ductwork?", "options": [ "create a pressure drop and regulate refrigerant flow", "compress and circulate refrigerant vapor", "transport air", "reduce airborne particulate matter" ], "answer": 2, "explanation": "The correct answer is transport air. It matches the defining characteristic or role described in the question.", "tags": [ "hvac" ], "status": "active" }, { "id": "HVAC-EASY-024-1", "category": "HVAC", "subcategory": "HVAC", "difficulty": "easy", "question": "Which term is best described by the following definition: a control or system that uses favorable outdoor conditions to reduce mechanical cooling?", "options": [ "SEER", "Economizer", "Compressor", "Ton of refrigeration" ], "answer": 1, "explanation": "The correct answer is Economizer. It matches the defining characteristic or role described in the question.", "tags": [ "hvac" ], "status": "active" }, { "id": "HVAC-MEDIUM-024-2", "category": "HVAC", "subcategory": "HVAC", "difficulty": "medium", "question": "Which statement best describes Economizer?", "options": [ "a control or system that uses favorable outdoor conditions to reduce mechanical cooling", "a British thermal unit, a traditional unit of heat energy", "Seasonal Energy Efficiency Ratio, a measure of seasonal cooling efficiency", "a component that removes particles from an airstream" ], "answer": 0, "explanation": "The correct answer is a control or system that uses favorable outdoor conditions to reduce mechanical cooling. It matches the defining characteristic or role described in the question.", "tags": [ "hvac" ], "status": "active" }, { "id": "HVAC-HARD-024-3", "category": "HVAC", "subcategory": "HVAC", "difficulty": "hard", "question": "A learner encounters this situation: cool outdoor air is used when conditions permit. Which concept best matches it?", "options": [ "Compressor", "Economizer", "BTU", "Expansion device" ], "answer": 1, "explanation": "The correct answer is Economizer. It matches the defining characteristic or role described in the question.", "tags": [ "hvac" ], "status": "active" }, { "id": "HVAC-HARD-024-4", "category": "HVAC", "subcategory": "HVAC", "difficulty": "hard", "question": "Which option best identifies the primary purpose or role associated with Economizer?", "options": [ "regulate conditioned-space temperature", "compress and circulate refrigerant vapor", "reduce airborne particulate matter", "reduce mechanical cooling energy" ], "answer": 3, "explanation": "The correct answer is reduce mechanical cooling energy. It matches the defining characteristic or role described in the question.", "tags": [ "hvac" ], "status": "active" }, { "id": "HVAC-EASY-025-1", "category": "HVAC", "subcategory": "HVAC", "difficulty": "easy", "question": "Which term is best described by the following definition: variable air volume, a system that varies supply airflow to zones?", "options": [ "Heat pump", "CFM", "BTU", "VAV" ], "answer": 3, "explanation": "The correct answer is VAV. It matches the defining characteristic or role described in the question.", "tags": [ "hvac" ], "status": "active" }, { "id": "HVAC-MEDIUM-025-2", "category": "HVAC", "subcategory": "HVAC", "difficulty": "medium", "question": "Which statement best describes VAV?", "options": [ "the ratio of actual water vapor pressure to saturation vapor pressure at the same temperature", "a system that can transfer heat in either direction depending on operating mode", "variable air volume, a system that varies supply airflow to zones", "temperature of vapor above its saturation temperature at a given pressure" ], "answer": 2, "explanation": "The correct answer is variable air volume, a system that varies supply airflow to zones. It matches the defining characteristic or role described in the question.", "tags": [ "hvac" ], "status": "active" }, { "id": "HVAC-HARD-025-3", "category": "HVAC", "subcategory": "HVAC", "difficulty": "hard", "question": "A learner encounters this situation: airflow to a zone changes according to demand. Which concept best matches it?", "options": [ "VAV", "Dew point", "Compressor", "Defrost cycle" ], "answer": 0, "explanation": "The correct answer is VAV. It matches the defining characteristic or role described in the question.", "tags": [ "hvac" ], "status": "active" }, { "id": "HVAC-EASY-025-4", "category": "HVAC", "subcategory": "HVAC", "difficulty": "easy", "question": "Which option best identifies the primary purpose or role associated with VAV?", "options": [ "predict condensation potential", "move heat between indoors and outdoors", "regulate conditioned-space temperature", "control zone conditioning efficiently" ], "answer": 3, "explanation": "The correct answer is control zone conditioning efficiently. It matches the defining characteristic or role described in the question.", "tags": [ "hvac" ], "status": "active" }, { "id": "IQLOGIC-000001", "category": "IQ & Logic", "subcategory": "Series", "difficulty": "easy", "question": "Look at this sequence: 5, 10, 15, 20, ___ . What comes next?", "options": [ "25", "30", "22", "35" ], "answer": 0, "explanation": "Pattern adds 5 each step: 20 + 5 = 25.", "tags": [ "iq & logic" ], "status": "active" }, { "id": "IQLOGIC-000002", "category": "IQ & Logic", "subcategory": "Riddles", "difficulty": "easy", "question": "A farmer has 15 sheep and all but 8 die. How many sheep are still alive?", "options": [ "8", "7", "0", "15" ], "answer": 0, "explanation": "All but 8 die means 8 survive.", "tags": [ "iq & logic" ], "status": "active" }, { "id": "IQLOGIC-000003", "category": "IQ & Logic", "subcategory": "Analogies", "difficulty": "easy", "question": "Puppy is to Dog as Kitten is to ___ ?", "options": [ "Cat", "Tiger", "Mouse", "Hamster" ], "answer": 0, "explanation": "A kitten is a young cat.", "tags": [ "iq & logic" ], "status": "active" }, { "id": "IQLOGIC-000004", "category": "IQ & Logic", "subcategory": "Patterns", "difficulty": "medium", "question": "What number comes next: 2, 6, 12, 20, 30, ___ ?", "options": [ "42", "40", "38", "48" ], "answer": 0, "explanation": "Differences increase by 2: +4, +6, +8, +10, +12 -> 30 + 12 = 42.", "tags": [ "iq & logic" ], "status": "active" }, { "id": "IQLOGIC-000005", "category": "IQ & Logic", "subcategory": "Logic", "difficulty": "medium", "question": "If yesterday was Tuesday, what day will it be 3 days after tomorrow?", "options": [ "Sunday", "Monday", "Saturday", "Friday" ], "answer": 0, "explanation": "Yesterday = Tue, Today = Wed, Tomorrow = Thu, +3 days = Sunday.", "tags": [ "iq & logic" ], "status": "active" }, { "id": "IQLOGIC-000006", "category": "IQ & Logic", "subcategory": "Math Logic", "difficulty": "medium", "question": "A bat and a ball cost $1.10 in total. The bat costs $1.00 more than the ball. How much does the ball cost?", "options": [ "$0.05 (5 cents)", "$0.10", "$0.15", "$0.01" ], "answer": 0, "explanation": "Ball = x; Bat = x + 1.00; 2x + 1.00 = 1.10; 2x = 0.10; x = $0.05.", "tags": [ "iq & logic" ], "status": "active" }, { "id": "IQLOGIC-000007", "category": "IQ & Logic", "subcategory": "Syllogisms", "difficulty": "hard", "question": "If all Bloops are Razzies, and all Razzies are Lizzies, which statement is guaranteed true?", "options": [ "All Bloops are Lizzies", "All Lizzies are Bloops", "No Bloops are Lizzies", "Some Bloops are not Lizzies" ], "answer": 0, "explanation": "By transitive logic, all Bloops are Lizzies.", "tags": [ "iq & logic" ], "status": "active" }, { "id": "IQLOGIC-000008", "category": "IQ & Logic", "subcategory": "Deduction", "difficulty": "hard", "question": "Four people (A, B, C, D) are in a race. A finishes ahead of B but behind C. D finishes ahead of C. Who won the race?", "options": [ "D", "C", "A", "B" ], "answer": 0, "explanation": "Order from first to last: D > C > A > B. D won the race.", "tags": [ "iq & logic" ], "status": "active" }, { "id": "IQLOGIC-000009", "category": "IQ & Logic", "subcategory": "Math Logic", "difficulty": "easy", "question": "If 3 cats can catch 3 mice in 3 minutes, how many cats are needed to catch 100 mice in 100 minutes?", "options": [ "3 cats", "100 cats", "33 cats", "30 cats" ], "answer": 0, "explanation": "1 cat catches 1 mouse in 3 minutes. In 100 minutes, 1 cat catches 33.3 mice; 3 cats catch 100 mice.", "tags": [ "iq & logic" ], "status": "active" }, { "id": "IQLOGIC-000010", "category": "IQ & Logic", "subcategory": "Patterns", "difficulty": "medium", "question": "What comes next in the letter sequence: J, F, M, A, M, J, ___ ?", "options": [ "J (July)", "A", "S", "O" ], "answer": 0, "explanation": "First letters of the months: January, February, March, April, May, June, July (J).", "tags": [ "iq & logic" ], "status": "active" }, { "id": "IQLOGIC-000011", "category": "IQ & Logic", "subcategory": "Probability", "difficulty": "hard", "question": "In the Monty Hall problem with 3 doors (1 car, 2 goats), what is your winning probability if you switch doors after a goat is revealed?", "options": [ "2/3 (approx 66.7%)", "1/2 (50%)", "1/3 (33.3%)", "3/4 (75%)" ], "answer": 0, "explanation": "Switching captures the initial 2/3 probability of picking a goat.", "tags": [ "iq & logic" ], "status": "active" }, { "id": "IQLOGIC-000012", "category": "IQ & Logic", "subcategory": "Patterns", "difficulty": "easy", "question": "Which word does not belong with the others: Apple, Orange, Banana, Carrot?", "options": [ "Carrot (it is a vegetable/root)", "Apple", "Orange", "Banana" ], "answer": 0, "explanation": "Carrot is a root vegetable; the others are fruits.", "tags": [ "iq & logic" ], "status": "active" }, { "id": "IQLOGIC-000013", "category": "IQ & Logic", "subcategory": "Math Riddle", "difficulty": "medium", "question": "If two's company, and three's a crowd, what are four and five?", "options": [ "9 (4 + 5 = 9)", "A party", "Ten", "Seven" ], "answer": 0, "explanation": "Four and five are 9 (classic wordplay riddle).", "tags": [ "iq & logic" ], "status": "active" }, { "id": "IQLOGIC-000014", "category": "IQ & Logic", "subcategory": "Logic", "difficulty": "hard", "question": "You have 8 identical-looking coins; 1 is lighter than the rest. What is the minimum weighings on a balance scale to find it?", "options": [ "2 weighings", "3 weighings", "4 weighings", "1 weighing" ], "answer": 0, "explanation": "Split into 3-3-2: Weigh 3 vs 3. If equal, weigh remaining 2. Total = 2 weighings.", "tags": [ "iq & logic" ], "status": "active" }, { "id": "MATH-000001", "category": "Mathematics", "subcategory": "Geometry", "difficulty": "easy", "question": "What is the formula for the area of a rectangle?", "options": [ "Area = Length × Width", "Area = 2L + 2W", "Area = L² × W²", "Area = (L+W)/2" ], "answer": 0, "explanation": "Area = Length × Width.", "tags": [ "mathematics" ], "status": "active" }, { "id": "MATH-000002", "category": "Mathematics", "subcategory": "Arithmetic", "difficulty": "easy", "question": "What is the square root of 144?", "options": [ "12", "14", "11", "16" ], "answer": 0, "explanation": "12 × 12 = 144.", "tags": [ "mathematics" ], "status": "active" }, { "id": "MATH-000003", "category": "Mathematics", "subcategory": "Fractions", "difficulty": "easy", "question": "What is 3/4 expressed as a percentage?", "options": [ "75%", "50%", "80%", "65%" ], "answer": 0, "explanation": "3 divided by 4 = 0.75 = 75%.", "tags": [ "mathematics" ], "status": "active" }, { "id": "MATH-000004", "category": "Mathematics", "subcategory": "Algebra", "difficulty": "medium", "question": "Solve for x: 3x + 15 = 36", "options": [ "x = 7", "x = 9", "x = 6", "x = 12" ], "answer": 0, "explanation": "3x = 21; x = 7.", "tags": [ "mathematics" ], "status": "active" }, { "id": "MATH-000005", "category": "Mathematics", "subcategory": "Statistics", "difficulty": "medium", "question": "What is the arithmetic mean (average) of 10, 20, 30, 40, and 50?", "options": [ "30", "25", "35", "40" ], "answer": 0, "explanation": "Sum = 150 / 5 = 30.", "tags": [ "mathematics" ], "status": "active" }, { "id": "MATH-000006", "category": "Mathematics", "subcategory": "Pythagoras", "difficulty": "medium", "question": "In a right triangle with legs of length 6 and 8, what is the length of the hypotenuse?", "options": [ "10", "14", "12", "9" ], "answer": 0, "explanation": "6² + 8² = 36 + 64 = 100; √100 = 10.", "tags": [ "mathematics" ], "status": "active" }, { "id": "MATH-000007", "category": "Mathematics", "subcategory": "Calculus", "difficulty": "hard", "question": "What is the derivative with respect to x of f(x) = 4x³ - 5x + 9?", "options": [ "f'(x) = 12x² - 5", "f'(x) = 12x² - 5x", "f'(x) = 4x² - 5", "f'(x) = 12x³ - 5" ], "answer": 0, "explanation": "d/dx[4x³ - 5x + 9] = 12x² - 5.", "tags": [ "mathematics" ], "status": "active" }, { "id": "MATH-000008", "category": "Mathematics", "subcategory": "Probability", "difficulty": "hard", "question": "What is the probability of rolling a total sum of 7 when rolling two standard 6-sided dice?", "options": [ "1/6 (6 out of 36 outcomes)", "1/12", "1/4", "1/8" ], "answer": 0, "explanation": "Combinations yielding 7: (1,6),(2,5),(3,4),(4,3),(5,2),(6,1) = 6/36 = 1/6.", "tags": [ "mathematics" ], "status": "active" }, { "id": "MATH-000009", "category": "Mathematics", "subcategory": "Trigonometry", "difficulty": "easy", "question": "In a right triangle, what is the trigonometric ratio of Sine of an acute angle?", "options": [ "Opposite / Hypotenuse", "Adjacent / Hypotenuse", "Opposite / Adjacent", "Hypotenuse / Opposite" ], "answer": 0, "explanation": "Sin = Opposite / Hypotenuse (SOH).", "tags": [ "mathematics" ], "status": "active" }, { "id": "MATH-000010", "category": "Mathematics", "subcategory": "Exponents", "difficulty": "medium", "question": "What is the value of 2^8?", "options": [ "256", "128", "512", "64" ], "answer": 0, "explanation": "2^8 = 256.", "tags": [ "mathematics" ], "status": "active" }, { "id": "MATH-000011", "category": "Mathematics", "subcategory": "Matrices", "difficulty": "hard", "question": "What is the determinant of a 2x2 matrix [[a, b], [c, d]]?", "options": [ "ad - bc", "ab - cd", "ac + bd", "ad + bc" ], "answer": 0, "explanation": "det(A) = ad - bc.", "tags": [ "mathematics" ], "status": "active" }, { "id": "MATH-000012", "category": "Mathematics", "subcategory": "Angles", "difficulty": "easy", "question": "What is the sum of interior angles in any geometric triangle?", "options": [ "180 degrees", "360 degrees", "90 degrees", "270 degrees" ], "answer": 0, "explanation": "Interior angles of any triangle sum to 180°.", "tags": [ "mathematics" ], "status": "active" }, { "id": "MATH-000013", "category": "Mathematics", "subcategory": "Logarithms", "difficulty": "medium", "question": "What is the value of log10(1,000)?", "options": [ "3", "10", "100", "4" ], "answer": 0, "explanation": "10^3 = 1,000, so log10(1000) = 3.", "tags": [ "mathematics" ], "status": "active" }, { "id": "MATH-000014", "category": "Mathematics", "subcategory": "Integrals", "difficulty": "hard", "question": "What is the indefinite integral ∫ 2x dx?", "options": [ "x² + C", "2x² + C", "x + C", "2 + C" ], "answer": 0, "explanation": "∫ 2x dx = x² + C.", "tags": [ "mathematics" ], "status": "active" }, { "id": "MEDTERM-000001", "category": "Medical Terminology", "subcategory": "Prefixes", "difficulty": "easy", "question": "What does the medical prefix 'Brady-' mean?", "options": [ "Slow", "Fast", "Difficult", "Excessive" ], "answer": 0, "explanation": "'Brady-' means slow.", "tags": [ "medical terminology" ], "status": "active" }, { "id": "MEDTERM-000002", "category": "Medical Terminology", "subcategory": "Prefixes", "difficulty": "easy", "question": "What does the medical prefix 'Tachy-' mean?", "options": [ "Fast / Rapid", "Slow", "Below", "Against" ], "answer": 0, "explanation": "'Tachy-' means fast.", "tags": [ "medical terminology" ], "status": "active" }, { "id": "MEDTERM-000003", "category": "Medical Terminology", "subcategory": "Prefixes", "difficulty": "easy", "question": "What does the prefix 'Hyper-' indicate?", "options": [ "Above / Excessive", "Below / Deficient", "Within", "Around" ], "answer": 0, "explanation": "'Hyper-' means above normal or excessive.", "tags": [ "medical terminology" ], "status": "active" }, { "id": "MEDTERM-000004", "category": "Medical Terminology", "subcategory": "Prefixes", "difficulty": "easy", "question": "What does the prefix 'Hypo-' indicate?", "options": [ "Below / Deficient", "Above", "Between", "Across" ], "answer": 0, "explanation": "'Hypo-' indicates deficient or below normal.", "tags": [ "medical terminology" ], "status": "active" }, { "id": "MEDTERM-000005", "category": "Medical Terminology", "subcategory": "Suffixes", "difficulty": "medium", "question": "What does the surgical suffix '-ectomy' indicate?", "options": [ "Surgical removal or excision", "Creating an artificial opening", "Surgical repair", "Endoscopic viewing" ], "answer": 0, "explanation": "'-ectomy' means surgical removal.", "tags": [ "medical terminology" ], "status": "active" }, { "id": "MEDTERM-000006", "category": "Medical Terminology", "subcategory": "Suffixes", "difficulty": "medium", "question": "What does the surgical suffix '-ostomy' signify?", "options": [ "Creating a new artificial opening", "Incision / cutting into", "Surgical repair", "Crushing of stone" ], "answer": 0, "explanation": "'-ostomy' creates an opening.", "tags": [ "medical terminology" ], "status": "active" }, { "id": "MEDTERM-000007", "category": "Medical Terminology", "subcategory": "Suffixes", "difficulty": "medium", "question": "What does the diagnostic suffix '-scopy' denote?", "options": [ "Visual examination with an instrument", "Surgical puncture to aspirate fluid", "Record or picture", "Incision into an organ" ], "answer": 0, "explanation": "'-scopy' means visual examination (e.g. endoscopy).", "tags": [ "medical terminology" ], "status": "active" }, { "id": 