as released Illmatic in 1994.", "tags": [ "music" ], "status": "active" }, { "id": "MUSIC-000009", "category": "Music", "subcategory": "Classical", "difficulty": "hard", "question": "In what musical form is a multi-movement orchestral composition typically structured in 4 movements?", "options": [ "Symphony", "Concerto", "Sonata", "Fugue" ], "answer": 0, "explanation": "Classical symphonies typically have four movements.", "tags": [ "music" ], "status": "active" }, { "id": "MUSIC-000010", "category": "Music", "subcategory": "Instruments", "difficulty": "easy", "question": "How many strings are on a standard acoustic or electric guitar?", "options": [ "6 strings", "4 strings", "5 strings", "8 strings" ], "answer": 0, "explanation": "A standard guitar has 6 strings (E-A-D-G-B-E).", "tags": [ "music" ], "status": "active" }, { "id": "MUSIC-000011", "category": "Music", "subcategory": "Rock", "difficulty": "medium", "question": "Which legendary rock band recorded the hits 'Stairway to Heaven' and 'Kashmir'?", "options": [ "Led Zeppelin", "The Who", "Deep Purple", "Black Sabbath" ], "answer": 0, "explanation": "Led Zeppelin released Stairway to Heaven in 1971.", "tags": [ "music" ], "status": "active" }, { "id": "MUSIC-000012", "category": "Music", "subcategory": "Classical", "difficulty": "hard", "question": "What famous Polish-French Romantic composer wrote almost exclusively for solo piano, including Nocturnes and Mazurkas?", "options": [ "Frederic Chopin", "Franz Liszt", "Claude Debussy", "Robert Schumann" ], "answer": 0, "explanation": "Frederic Chopin is the poetic master of Romantic solo piano.", "tags": [ "music" ], "status": "active" }, { "id": "NCLEX-000001", "category": "NCLEX", "subcategory": "Fundamentals", "difficulty": "easy", "question": "What is the normal resting adult pulse rate range?", "options": [ "60 to 100 beats/min", "40-60 bpm", "100-140 bpm", "50-70 bpm" ], "answer": 0, "explanation": "Normal resting adult pulse is 60 to 100 bpm.", "tags": [ "nclex" ], "status": "active" }, { "id": "NCLEX-000002", "category": "NCLEX", "subcategory": "Infection Control", "difficulty": "easy", "question": "Which PPE is donned first for contact precautions?", "options": [ "Clean isolation gown", "Gloves", "N95 mask", "Shoe covers" ], "answer": 0, "explanation": "Gown is donned first, followed by mask, eye protection, and gloves.", "tags": [ "nclex" ], "status": "active" }, { "id": "NCLEX-000003", "category": "NCLEX", "subcategory": "Safety", "difficulty": "easy", "question": "Which two client identifiers are required before medication administration?", "options": [ "Full name and date of birth", "Room and bed number", "Diagnosis and room", "Doctor name and badge" ], "answer": 0, "explanation": "Full name and DOB or MRN are standard.", "tags": [ "nclex" ], "status": "active" }, { "id": "NCLEX-000004", "category": "NCLEX", "subcategory": "Respiratory", "difficulty": "easy", "question": "What is the normal resting adult respiratory rate range?", "options": [ "12 to 20 breaths/min", "8-10 bpm", "24-32 bpm", "30-40 bpm" ], "answer": 0, "explanation": "Normal adult resting rate is 12-20 bpm.", "tags": [ "nclex" ], "status": "active" }, { "id": "NCLEX-000005", "category": "NCLEX", "subcategory": "Positioning", "difficulty": "easy", "question": "Which position is best to prevent aspiration during oral meals?", "options": [ "High Fowler's (90 degrees)", "Supine flat", "Trendelenburg", "Left lateral" ], "answer": 0, "explanation": "High Fowler's facilitates safe swallowing.", "tags": [ "nclex" ], "status": "active" }, { "id": "NCLEX-000006", "category": "NCLEX", "subcategory": "Oxygen", "difficulty": "easy", "question": "What is the maximum flow rate for a standard nasal cannula in L/min?", "options": [ "6 L/min", "15 L/min", "25 L/min", "2 L/min" ], "answer": 0, "explanation": "Standard nasal cannula flow is 1-6 L/min.", "tags": [ "nclex" ], "status": "active" }, { "id": "NCLEX-000007", "category": "NCLEX", "subcategory": "Renal", "difficulty": "easy", "question": "What is minimum expected hourly urine output in an adult?", "options": [ "30 mL/hr", "5 mL/hr", "100 mL/hr", "10 mL/hr" ], "answer": 0, "explanation": "Hourly output < 30 mL/hr signals oliguria.", "tags": [ "nclex" ], "status": "active" }, { "id": "NCLEX-000008", "category": "NCLEX", "subcategory": "Post-op", "difficulty": "easy", "question": "How often should an awake post-op client use an incentive spirometer?", "options": [ "10 times every hour", "Once every 8 hours", "Twice a day", "Only when coughing" ], "answer": 0, "explanation": "10 times per hour prevents atelectasis.", "tags": [ "nclex" ], "status": "active" }, { "id": "NCLEX-000009", "category": "NCLEX", "subcategory": "Cardiology", "difficulty": "medium", "question": "A patient taking Digoxin has an apical pulse of 52 bpm. What is the priority nursing action?", "options": [ "Withhold the dose and notify provider", "Give dose with water", "Double dose tomorrow", "Encourage exercise" ], "answer": 0, "explanation": "Withhold digoxin if apical HR < 60 bpm.", "tags": [ "nclex" ], "status": "active" }, { "id": "NCLEX-000010", "category": "NCLEX", "subcategory": "Maternal", "difficulty": "medium", "question": "Four hours postpartum, a client's fundus is boggy and deviated right. What is the first action?", "options": [ "Assist client to void or catheterize", "Massage fundus with high pressure", "Give IV oxytocin", "Place in Trendelenburg" ], "answer": 0, "explanation": "Deviation to the right indicates full bladder.", "tags": [ "nclex" ], "status": "active" }, { "id": "NCLEX-000011", "category": "NCLEX", "subcategory": "Endocrine", "difficulty": "medium", "question": "A diabetic client exhibits shakiness, sweating, and confusion. What is the immediate treatment?", "options": [ "Provide 15g fast-acting carbohydrates", "Give 10 units regular insulin", "Place in Trendelenburg", "Withhold fluids" ], "answer": 0, "explanation": "Hypoglycemia requires 15g fast carbs.", "tags": [ "nclex" ], "status": "active" }, { "id": "NCLEX-000012", "category": "NCLEX", "subcategory": "Fluids", "difficulty": "medium", "question": "Which IV fluid is isotonic with plasma and standard for resuscitation?", "options": [ "0.9% Normal Saline", "0.45% Saline", "3% Saline", "Dextrose 10%" ], "answer": 0, "explanation": "0.9% Normal Saline is isotonic.", "tags": [ "nclex" ], "status": "active" }, { "id": "NCLEX-000013", "category": "NCLEX", "subcategory": "Delegation", "difficulty": "medium", "question": "Which task can be safely delegated to an unlicensed assistive personnel (UAP)?", "options": [ "Measuring routine intake and output", "Assessing a central line", "Discharge teaching", "Giving oral pain meds" ], "answer": 0, "explanation": "UAPs can measure routine intake and output.", "tags": [ "nclex" ], "status": "active" }, { "id": "NCLEX-000014", "category": "NCLEX", "subcategory": "Anticoagulation", "difficulty": "medium", "question": "Which lab test is used to monitor continuous IV Heparin therapy?", "options": [ "aPTT (Activated Partial Thromboplastin Time)", "INR", "Platelet factor 4", "Bleeding time" ], "answer": 0, "explanation": "aPTT monitors Heparin; INR monitors Warfarin.", "tags": [ "nclex" ], "status": "active" }, { "id": "NCLEX-000015", "category": "NCLEX", "subcategory": "Prioritization", "difficulty": "hard", "question": "Which client should the nurse assess first after change-of-shift report?", "options": [ "Asthmatic whose loud wheezing suddenly becomes silent", "Diabetic with glucose of 185 mg/dL", "Post-op knee with 7/10 pain", "CKD with creatinine 2.8 mg/dL" ], "answer": 0, "explanation": "Silent chest indicates impending respiratory arrest.", "tags": [ "nclex" ], "status": "active" }, { "id": "NCLEX-000016", "category": "NCLEX", "subcategory": "Neurology", "difficulty": "hard", "question": "A client with ICP of 24 mmHg is in bed. Which intervention is contraindicated?", "options": [ "Trendelenburg position", "Elevating head of bed 30 degrees", "Administering mannitol IV", "Maintaining neutral neck alignment" ], "answer": 0, "explanation": "Trendelenburg elevates ICP.", "tags": [ "nclex" ], "status": "active" }, { "id": "NCLEX-000017", "category": "NCLEX", "subcategory": "Hemodynamics", "difficulty": "hard", "question": "Which triad indicates impending brain herniation from severe intracranial pressure?", "options": [ "Cushing's Triad (Widening pulse pressure, bradycardia, irregular respirations)", "Beck's Triad", "Charcot's Triad", "Virchow's Triad" ], "answer": 0, "explanation": "Cushing's Triad signifies severe ICP elevation.", "tags": [ "nclex" ], "status": "active" }, { "id": "NCLEX-000018", "category": "NCLEX", "subcategory": "Acid-Base", "difficulty": "hard", "question": "ABG results: pH 7.28, PaCO2 56 mmHg, HCO3 25 mEq/L. What is the interpretation?", "options": [ "Uncompensated Respiratory Acidosis", "Compensated Metabolic Acidosis", "Uncompensated Metabolic Alkalosis", "Compensated Respiratory Alkalosis" ], "answer": 0, "explanation": "Low pH with high PaCO2 and normal HCO3 is uncompensated respiratory acidosis.", "tags": [ "nclex" ], "status": "active" }, { "id": "NCLEX-000019", "category": "NCLEX", "subcategory": "Pharmacology", "difficulty": "hard", "question": "A client on Lithium presents with coarse tremors, persistent vomiting, confusion, and ataxia. What is the priority?", "options": [ "Hold lithium and notify physician immediately for serum level", "Give next dose with food", "Restrict dietary sodium", "Encourage exercise" ], "answer": 0, "explanation": "Coarse tremors and ataxia indicate lithium toxicity.", "tags": [ "nclex" ], "status": "active" }, { "id": "NCLEX-000020", "category": "NCLEX", "subcategory": "Shock", "difficulty": "hard", "question": "In neurogenic shock from spinal injury above T6, which hemodynamic profile is observed?", "options": [ "Hypotension with Bradycardia and warm, dry skin", "Hypotension with Tachycardia and cold skin", "Hypertension with Tachycardia", "Hypertension with Tachypnea" ], "answer": 0, "explanation": "Loss of sympathetic tone causes vasodilation and bradycardia.", "tags": [ "nclex" ], "status": "active" }, { "id": "NCLEX-000021", "category": "NCLEX", "subcategory": "Pediatrics", "difficulty": "easy", "question": "At what age does the anterior fontanelle typically close in a healthy infant?", "options": [ "12 to 18 months", "2 to 3 months", "6 to 8 months", "24 to 36 months" ], "answer": 0, "explanation": "The anterior fontanelle closes between 12-18 months; posterior fontanelle closes at 2-3 months.", "tags": [ "nclex" ], "status": "active" }, { "id": "NCLEX-000022", "category": "NCLEX", "subcategory": "Medication Admin", "difficulty": "medium", "question": "When administering ear drops (otic solution) to a 2-year-old child, in which direction should the pinna be pulled?", "options": [ "Down and back", "Up and back", "Straight forward", "Directly inward" ], "answer": 0, "explanation": "For children under 3 years, pull pinna down and back. For older children and adults, pull up and back.", "tags": [ "nclex" ], "status": "active" }, { "id": "NCLEX-000023", "category": "NCLEX", "subcategory": "Critical Care", "difficulty": "hard", "question": "A client with acute myocardial infarction develops sudden pulmonary edema and a new holosystolic apical murmur. What mechanical complication is suspected?", "options": [ "Acute Mitral Valve Papillary Muscle Rupture", "Ventricular Septal Aneurysm", "Cardiac Tamponade", "Aortic Dissection" ], "answer": 0, "explanation": "Papillary muscle rupture post-MI causes acute severe mitral regurgitation and flash pulmonary edema.", "tags": [ "nclex" ], "status": "active" }, { "id": "NCLEX-000024", "category": "NCLEX", "subcategory": "Maternal", "difficulty": "easy", "question": "What is the normal fetal heart rate (FHR) baseline range in beats per minute?", "options": [ "110 to 160 bpm", "80 to 100 bpm", "170 to 200 bpm", "60 to 90 bpm" ], "answer": 0, "explanation": "Normal baseline fetal heart rate is 110-160 bpm.", "tags": [ "nclex" ], "status": "active" }, { "id": "NCLEX-000025", "category": "NCLEX", "subcategory": "Mental Health", "difficulty": "medium", "question": "When interacting with a client experiencing auditory hallucinations, what is the best therapeutic response?", "options": [ "'I know the voices seem real to you, but I do not hear any voices.'", "'Tell the voices to leave right now.'", "'Why are you making up stories?'", "'What are the voices planning to do?'" ], "answer": 0, "explanation": "Acknowledge the client's feelings while stating reality without validating hallucinations.", "tags": [ "nclex" ], "status": "active" }, { "id": "NCLEX-000026", "category": "NCLEX", "subcategory": "Orthopedics", "difficulty": "hard", "question": "A client in skeletal traction reports sudden severe calf pain and warmth. What is the priority concern?", "options": [ "Deep Vein Thrombosis (DVT)", "Normal pin-site pain", "Compartment syndrome in foot", "Fat embolism syndrome" ], "answer": 0, "explanation": "Unilateral calf pain, swelling, and warmth in immobilized traction clients indicate DVT.", "tags": [ "nclex" ], "status": "active" }, { "id": "NCLEX-EASY-001-1", "category": "NCLEX", "subcategory": "NCLEX", "difficulty": "easy", "question": "Which term is best described by the following definition: maintenance of a patent airway is a fundamental immediate priority?", "options": [ "Priority assessment", "Airway priority", "ABCs", "Discharge planning" ], "answer": 1, "explanation": "The correct answer is Airway priority. It matches the defining characteristic or role described in the question.", "tags": [ "nclex" ], "status": "active" }, { "id": "NCLEX-MEDIUM-001-2", "category": "NCLEX", "subcategory": "NCLEX", "difficulty": "medium", "question": "Which statement best describes Airway priority?", "options": [ "maintenance of a patent airway is a fundamental immediate priority", "worsening physiologic status requiring prompt recognition and action", "likelihood that a patient may fall and sustain injury", "recognition of infection with systemic physiologic deterioration" ], "answer": 0, "explanation": "The correct answer is maintenance of a patent airway is a fundamental immediate priority. It matches the defining characteristic or role described in the question.", "tags": [ "nclex" ], "status": "active" }, { "id": "NCLEX-HARD-001-3", "category": "NCLEX", "subcategory": "NCLEX", "difficulty": "hard", "question": "A learner encounters this situation: a patient has severe airway obstruction. Which concept best matches it?", "options": [ "ABCs", "Discharge planning", "Stroke warning signs", "Airway priority" ], "answer": 3, "explanation": "The correct answer is Airway priority. It matches the defining characteristic or role described in the question.", "tags": [ "nclex" ], "status": "active" }, { "id": "NCLEX-EASY-001-4", "category": "NCLEX", "subcategory": "NCLEX", "difficulty": "easy", "question": "Which option best identifies the primary purpose or role associated with Airway priority?", "options": [ "support safe team-based care", "prioritize care based on urgency", "restore or protect the airway first", "prevent avoidable medication errors" ], "answer": 2, "explanation": "The correct answer is restore or protect the airway first. It matches the defining characteristic or role described in the question.", "tags": [ "nclex" ], "status": "active" }, { "id": "NCLEX-EASY-002-1", "category": "NCLEX", "subcategory": "NCLEX", "difficulty": "easy", "question": "Which term is best described by the following definition: airway, breathing, and circulation?", "options": [ "ABCs", "Stroke warning signs", "Airway priority", "Chest pain priority" ], "answer": 0, "explanation": "The correct answer is ABCs. It matches the defining characteristic or role described in the question.", "tags": [ "nclex" ], "status": "active" }, { "id": "NCLEX-MEDIUM-002-2", "category": "NCLEX", "subcategory": "NCLEX", "difficulty": "medium", "question": "Which statement best describes ABCs?", "options": [ "a finding consistent with the known condition or intervention", "maintenance of a patent airway is a fundamental immediate priority", "rapid recognition of symptoms associated with low blood glucose", "airway, breathing, and circulation" ], "answer": 3, "explanation": "The correct answer is airway, breathing, and circulation. It matches the defining characteristic or role described in the question.", "tags": [ "nclex" ], "status": "active" }, { "id": "NCLEX-HARD-002-3", "category": "NCLEX", "subcategory": "NCLEX", "difficulty": "hard", "question": "A learner encounters this situation: a nurse prioritizes several competing patient problems. Which concept best matches it?", "options": [ "Patient teaching", "Fluid balance", "Expected finding", "ABCs" ], "answer": 3, "explanation": "The correct answer is ABCs. It matches the defining characteristic or role described in the question.", "tags": [ "nclex" ], "status": "active" }, { "id": "NCLEX-MEDIUM-002-4", "category": "NCLEX", "subcategory": "NCLEX", "difficulty": "medium", "question": "Which option best identifies the primary purpose or role associated with ABCs?", "options": [ "prioritize care based on urgency", "ensure the task and follow-up are appropriate", "organize urgent assessment and intervention priorities", "recognize and report treatment-related harm" ], "answer": 2, "explanation": "The correct answer is organize urgent assessment and intervention priorities. It matches the defining characteristic or role described in the question.", "tags": [ "nclex" ], "status": "active" }, { "id": "NCLEX-EASY-003-1", "category": "NCLEX", "subcategory": "NCLEX", "difficulty": "easy", "question": "Which term is best described by the following definition: sorting patients according to urgency and resource needs?", "options": [ "Triage", "Hypoglycemia response", "Stroke warning signs", "Chest pain priority" ], "answer": 0, "explanation": "The correct answer is Triage. It matches the defining characteristic or role described in the question.", "tags": [ "nclex" ], "status": "active" }, { "id": "NCLEX-MEDIUM-003-2", "category": "NCLEX", "subcategory": "NCLEX", "difficulty": "medium", "question": "Which statement best describes Triage?", "options": [ "airway, breathing, and circulation", "worsening physiologic status requiring prompt recognition and action", "sorting patients according to urgency and resource needs", "abnormal concentration of electrolytes such as sodium or potassium" ], "answer": 2, "explanation": "The correct answer is sorting patients according to urgency and resource needs. It matches the defining characteristic or role described in the question.", "tags": [ "nclex" ], "status": "active" }, { "id": "NCLEX-HARD-003-3", "category": "NCLEX", "subcategory": "NCLEX", "difficulty": "hard", "question": "A learner encounters this situation: multiple patients arrive with different levels of acuity. Which concept best matches it?", "options": [ "Triage", "Fluid balance", "Airborne precautions", "Stroke warning signs" ], "answer": 0, "explanation": "The correct answer is Triage. It matches the defining characteristic or role described in the question.", "tags": [ "nclex" ], "status": "active" }, { "id": "NCLEX-HARD-003-4", "category": "NCLEX", "subcategory": "NCLEX", "difficulty": "hard", "question": "Which option best identifies the primary purpose or role associated with Triage?", "options": [ "ensure the task and follow-up are appropriate", "promote safe self-management", "reduce preventable problems after discharge", "prioritize care based on urgency" ], "answer": 3, "explanation": "The correct answer is prioritize care based on urgency. It matches the defining characteristic or role described in the question.", "tags": [ "nclex" ], "status": "active" }, { "id": "NCLEX-EASY-004-1", "category": "NCLEX", "subcategory": "NCLEX", "difficulty": "easy", "question": "Which term is best described by the following definition: tasks should be delegated according to patient stability, task complexity, and team member competence?", "options": [ "Airway priority", "Delegation principles", "Expected finding", "Clinical deterioration" ], "answer": 1, "explanation": "The correct answer is Delegation principles. It matches the defining characteristic or role described in the question.", "tags": [ "nclex" ], "status": "active" }, { "id": "NCLEX-MEDIUM-004-2", "category": "NCLEX", "subcategory": "NCLEX", "difficulty": "medium", "question": "Which statement best describes Delegation principles?", "options": [ "tasks should be delegated according to patient stability, task complexity, and team member competence", "abnormal concentration of electrolytes such as sodium or potassium", "sudden neurologic changes such as facial droop, arm weakness, or speech difficulty", "precautions for pathogens capable of remaining suspended in the air" ], "answer": 0, "explanation": "The correct answer is tasks should be delegated according to patient stability, task complexity, and team member competence. It matches the defining characteristic or role described in the question.", "tags": [ "nclex" ], "status": "active" }, { "id": "NCLEX-HARD-004-3", "category": "NCLEX", "subcategory": "NCLEX", "difficulty": "hard", "question": "A learner encounters this situation: a nurse considers which task can safely be assigned. Which concept best matches it?", "options": [ "Adverse reaction", "Priority assessment", "Delegation principles", "Fluid balance" ], "answer": 2, "explanation": "The correct answer is Delegation principles. It matches the defining characteristic or role described in the question.", "tags": [ "nclex" ], "status": "active" }, { "id": "NCLEX-EASY-004-4", "category": "NCLEX", "subcategory": "NCLEX", "difficulty": "easy", "question": "Which option best identifies the primary purpose or role associated with Delegation principles?", "options": [ "prioritize care based on urgency", "implement appropriate safety measures", "support safe team-based care", "identify an unstable patient early" ], "answer": 2, "explanation": "The correct answer is support safe team-based care. It matches the defining characteristic or role described in the question.", "tags": [ "nclex" ], "status": "active" }, { "id": "NCLEX-EASY-005-1", "category": "NCLEX", "subcategory": "NCLEX", "difficulty": "easy", "question": "Which term is best described by the following definition: practices that reduce medication errors?", "options": [ "Chest pain priority", "Triage", "Fall risk", "Medication safety" ], "answer": 3, "explanation": "The correct answer is Medication safety. It matches the defining characteristic or role described in the question.", "tags": [ "nclex" ], "status": "active" }, { "id": "NCLEX-MEDIUM-005-2", "category": "NCLEX", "subcategory": "NCLEX", "difficulty": "medium", "question": "Which statement best describes Medication safety?", "options": [ "likelihood that a patient may fall and sustain injury", "practices that reduce medication errors", "education that helps patients understand and safely manage their care", "a finding consistent with the known condition or intervention" ], "answer": 1, "explanation": "The correct answer is practices that reduce medication errors. It matches the defining characteristic or role described in the question.", "tags": [ "nclex" ], "status": "active" }, { "id": "NCLEX-HARD-005-3", "category": "NCLEX", "subcategory": "NCLEX", "difficulty": "hard", "question": "A learner encounters this situation: a nurse verifies the patient, medication, dose, route, and timing. Which concept best matches it?", "options": [ "Medication safety", "Triage", "Contact precautions", "Priority assessment" ], "answer": 0, "explanation": "The correct answer is Medication safety. It matches the defining characteristic or role described in the question.", "tags": [ "nclex" ], "status": "active" }, { "id": "NCLEX-MEDIUM-005-4", "category": "NCLEX", "subcategory": "NCLEX", "d