ed first on the most immediate threat to life or safety", "new or severe chest pain may indicate a time-sensitive cardiovascular emergency", "abnormal concentration of electrolytes such as sodium or potassium" ], "answer": 1, "explanation": "The correct answer is assessment focused first on the most immediate threat to life or safety. It matches the defining characteristic or role described in the question.", "tags": [ "nclex" ], "status": "active" }, { "id": "NCLEX-HARD-021-3", "category": "NCLEX", "subcategory": "NCLEX", "difficulty": "hard", "question": "A learner encounters this situation: several findings compete for attention. Which concept best matches it?", "options": [ "Fluid balance", "Isolation precautions", "Priority assessment", "Contact precautions" ], "answer": 2, "explanation": "The correct answer is Priority assessment. It matches the defining characteristic or role described in the question.", "tags": [ "nclex" ], "status": "active" }, { "id": "NCLEX-HARD-021-4", "category": "NCLEX", "subcategory": "NCLEX", "difficulty": "hard", "question": "Which option best identifies the primary purpose or role associated with Priority assessment?", "options": [ "prevent avoidable medication errors", "identify the most urgent problem", "trigger urgent stroke evaluation", "implement appropriate safety measures" ], "answer": 1, "explanation": "The correct answer is identify the most urgent problem. It matches the defining characteristic or role described in the question.", "tags": [ "nclex" ], "status": "active" }, { "id": "NCLEX-EASY-022-1", "category": "NCLEX", "subcategory": "NCLEX", "difficulty": "easy", "question": "Which term is best described by the following definition: a finding consistent with the known condition or intervention?", "options": [ "Airway priority", "Contact precautions", "Expected finding", "Priority assessment" ], "answer": 2, "explanation": "The correct answer is Expected finding. It matches the defining characteristic or role described in the question.", "tags": [ "nclex" ], "status": "active" }, { "id": "NCLEX-MEDIUM-022-2", "category": "NCLEX", "subcategory": "NCLEX", "difficulty": "medium", "question": "Which statement best describes Expected finding?", "options": [ "precautions for pathogens capable of remaining suspended in the air", "measures selected according to the mode of pathogen transmission", "precautions for infections spread through respiratory droplets", "a finding consistent with the known condition or intervention" ], "answer": 3, "explanation": "The correct answer is a finding consistent with the known condition or intervention. It matches the defining characteristic or role described in the question.", "tags": [ "nclex" ], "status": "active" }, { "id": "NCLEX-HARD-022-3", "category": "NCLEX", "subcategory": "NCLEX", "difficulty": "hard", "question": "A learner encounters this situation: a question asks which assessment result is anticipated. Which concept best matches it?", "options": [ "Hypoglycemia response", "Airway priority", "Delegation principles", "Expected finding" ], "answer": 3, "explanation": "The correct answer is Expected finding. It matches the defining characteristic or role described in the question.", "tags": [ "nclex" ], "status": "active" }, { "id": "NCLEX-EASY-022-4", "category": "NCLEX", "subcategory": "NCLEX", "difficulty": "easy", "question": "Which option best identifies the primary purpose or role associated with Expected finding?", "options": [ "evaluate hydration and volume status", "reduce preventable problems after discharge", "trigger urgent stroke evaluation", "distinguish expected from concerning findings" ], "answer": 3, "explanation": "The correct answer is distinguish expected from concerning findings. It matches the defining characteristic or role described in the question.", "tags": [ "nclex" ], "status": "active" }, { "id": "NCLEX-EASY-023-1", "category": "NCLEX", "subcategory": "NCLEX", "difficulty": "easy", "question": "Which term is best described by the following definition: an unintended harmful response to a medication or treatment?", "options": [ "Delegation principles", "Adverse reaction", "Airway priority", "Sepsis recognition" ], "answer": 1, "explanation": "The correct answer is Adverse reaction. It matches the defining characteristic or role described in the question.", "tags": [ "nclex" ], "status": "active" }, { "id": "NCLEX-MEDIUM-023-2", "category": "NCLEX", "subcategory": "NCLEX", "difficulty": "medium", "question": "Which statement best describes Adverse reaction?", "options": [ "tasks should be delegated according to patient stability, task complexity, and team member competence", "precautions for infections spread through respiratory droplets", "an unintended harmful response to a medication or treatment", "sorting patients according to urgency and resource needs" ], "answer": 2, "explanation": "The correct answer is an unintended harmful response to a medication or treatment. It matches the defining characteristic or role described in the question.", "tags": [ "nclex" ], "status": "active" }, { "id": "NCLEX-HARD-023-3", "category": "NCLEX", "subcategory": "NCLEX", "difficulty": "hard", "question": "A learner encounters this situation: a patient develops a concerning symptom after medication administration. Which concept best matches it?", "options": [ "Adverse reaction", "Informed consent", "Droplet precautions", "Stroke warning signs" ], "answer": 0, "explanation": "The correct answer is Adverse reaction. It matches the defining characteristic or role described in the question.", "tags": [ "nclex" ], "status": "active" }, { "id": "NCLEX-MEDIUM-023-4", "category": "NCLEX", "subcategory": "NCLEX", "difficulty": "medium", "question": "Which option best identifies the primary purpose or role associated with Adverse reaction?", "options": [ "encourage expression and gather useful information", "reduce droplet exposure", "restore or protect the airway first", "recognize and report treatment-related harm" ], "answer": 3, "explanation": "The correct answer is recognize and report treatment-related harm. It matches the defining characteristic or role described in the question.", "tags": [ "nclex" ], "status": "active" }, { "id": "NCLEX-EASY-024-1", "category": "NCLEX", "subcategory": "NCLEX", "difficulty": "easy", "question": "Which term is best described by the following definition: education that helps patients understand and safely manage their care?", "options": [ "Therapeutic communication", "Medication safety", "Patient teaching", "Chest pain priority" ], "answer": 2, "explanation": "The correct answer is Patient teaching. It matches the defining characteristic or role described in the question.", "tags": [ "nclex" ], "status": "active" }, { "id": "NCLEX-MEDIUM-024-2", "category": "NCLEX", "subcategory": "NCLEX", "difficulty": "medium", "question": "Which statement best describes Patient teaching?", "options": [ "likelihood that a patient may fall and sustain injury", "sorting patients according to urgency and resource needs", "measures selected according to the mode of pathogen transmission", "education that helps patients understand and safely manage their care" ], "answer": 3, "explanation": "The correct answer is education that helps patients understand and safely manage their care. It matches the defining characteristic or role described in the question.", "tags": [ "nclex" ], "status": "active" }, { "id": "NCLEX-HARD-024-3", "category": "NCLEX", "subcategory": "NCLEX", "difficulty": "hard", "question": "A learner encounters this situation: a nurse explains how to take a medication at home. Which concept best matches it?", "options": [ "Fall risk", "Sepsis recognition", "Patient teaching", "Delegation accountability" ], "answer": 2, "explanation": "The correct answer is Patient teaching. It matches the defining characteristic or role described in the question.", "tags": [ "nclex" ], "status": "active" }, { "id": "NCLEX-HARD-024-4", "category": "NCLEX", "subcategory": "NCLEX", "difficulty": "hard", "question": "Which option best identifies the primary purpose or role associated with Patient teaching?", "options": [ "promote safe self-management", "support patient autonomy", "reduce droplet exposure", "perform prompt assessment and escalation" ], "answer": 0, "explanation": "The correct answer is promote safe self-management. It matches the defining characteristic or role described in the question.", "tags": [ "nclex" ], "status": "active" }, { "id": "NCLEX-EASY-025-1", "category": "NCLEX", "subcategory": "NCLEX", "difficulty": "easy", "question": "Which term is best described by the following definition: planning that prepares a patient for safe care after leaving a healthcare setting?", "options": [ "Delegation principles", "Expected finding", "Fall risk", "Discharge planning" ], "answer": 3, "explanation": "The correct answer is Discharge planning. It matches the defining characteristic or role described in the question.", "tags": [ "nclex" ], "status": "active" }, { "id": "NCLEX-MEDIUM-025-2", "category": "NCLEX", "subcategory": "NCLEX", "difficulty": "medium", "question": "Which statement best describes Discharge planning?", "options": [ "airway, breathing, and circulation", "communication focused on the patient's needs rather than the nurse's personal reactions", "assessment focused first on the most immediate threat to life or safety", "planning that prepares a patient for safe care after leaving a healthcare setting" ], "answer": 3, "explanation": "The correct answer is planning that prepares a patient for safe care after leaving a healthcare setting. It matches the defining characteristic or role described in the question.", "tags": [ "nclex" ], "status": "active" }, { "id": "NCLEX-HARD-025-3", "category": "NCLEX", "subcategory": "NCLEX", "difficulty": "hard", "question": "A learner encounters this situation: a patient needs follow-up, medication instructions, and home support. Which concept best matches it?", "options": [ "Airborne precautions", "Discharge planning", "Electrolyte imbalance", "Sepsis recognition" ], "answer": 1, "explanation": "The correct answer is Discharge planning. It matches the defining characteristic or role described in the question.", "tags": [ "nclex" ], "status": "active" }, { "id": "NCLEX-EASY-025-4", "category": "NCLEX", "subcategory": "NCLEX", "difficulty": "easy", "question": "Which option best identifies the primary purpose or role associated with Discharge planning?", "options": [ "reduce preventable problems after discharge", "reduce airborne transmission", "prioritize care based on urgency", "limit transmission" ], "answer": 0, "explanation": "The correct answer is reduce preventable problems after discharge. It matches the defining characteristic or role described in the question.", "tags": [ "nclex" ], "status": "active" }, { "id": "NURS-000001", "category": "Nursing", "subcategory": "Infection Control", "difficulty": "easy", "question": "What is the single most effective action to prevent healthcare-associated infections?", "options": [ "Hand hygiene before and after patient contact", "Double gloving", "Prophylactic antibiotics", "Wiping doors daily" ], "answer": 0, "explanation": "Hand hygiene is the gold standard.", "tags": [ "nursing" ], "status": "active" }, { "id": "NURS-000002", "category": "Nursing", "subcategory": "Skin Care", "difficulty": "easy", "question": "What characterizes a Stage 1 pressure injury?", "options": [ "Non-blanchable erythema of intact skin", "Partial-thickness dermis loss", "Full-thickness fat exposure", "Exposed bone and tendon" ], "answer": 0, "explanation": "Stage 1 is non-blanchable redness on intact skin.", "tags": [ "nursing" ], "status": "active" }, { "id": "NURS-000003", "category": "Nursing", "subcategory": "Ethics", "difficulty": "easy", "question": "Honoring a patient's informed refusal of medical treatment demonstrates which principle?", "options": [ "Autonomy", "Beneficence", "Non-maleficence", "Justice" ], "answer": 0, "explanation": "Autonomy respects patient self-determination.", "tags": [ "nursing" ], "status": "active" }, { "id": "NURS-000004", "category": "Nursing", "subcategory": "Communication", "difficulty": "easy", "question": "What does SBAR stand for in clinical handoff communication?", "options": [ "Situation, Background, Assessment, Recommendation", "Safety, Baseline, Action, Response", "Subjective, Bedside, Analysis, Review", "Sign, Behavior, Action, Result" ], "answer": 0, "explanation": "SBAR standardizes clinical communication.", "tags": [ "nursing" ], "status": "active" }, { "id": "NURS-000005", "category": "Nursing", "subcategory": "Mobility", "difficulty": "easy", "question": "How frequently should bedbound clients be repositioned?", "options": [ "Every 2 hours", "Every 6 hours", "Every 8 hours", "Once a day" ], "answer": 0, "explanation": "Repositioning every 2 hours prevents pressure ulcers.", "tags": [ "nursing" ], "status": "active" }, { "id": "NURS-000006", "category": "Nursing", "subcategory": "Vitals", "difficulty": "easy", "question": "Where is the apical pulse auscultated in an adult?", "options": [ "5th intercostal space, left midclavicular line", "2nd intercostal space, right sternal border", "4th intercostal space, right midclavicular line", "6th intercostal space, anterior axillary line" ], "answer": 0, "explanation": "Apical pulse is at the 5th intercostal space left midclavicular line.", "tags": [ "nursing" ], "status": "active" }, { "id": "NURS-000007", "category": "Nursing", "subcategory": "Respiratory", "difficulty": "medium", "question": "Which position is best to relieve acute dyspnea and maximize lung expansion?", "options": [ "High Fowler's position", "Trendelenburg", "Prone", "Supine" ], "answer": 0, "explanation": "High Fowler's lowers the diaphragm for maximum thoracic expansion.", "tags": [ "nursing" ], "status": "active" }, { "id": "NURS-000008", "category": "Nursing", "subcategory": "Injections", "difficulty": "medium", "question": "What is the preferred intramuscular injection site for volumes over 1 mL in adults?", "options": [ "Ventrogluteal site", "Dorsogluteal site", "Deltoid muscle", "Vastus medialis" ], "answer": 0, "explanation": "Ventrogluteal is free of major nerves.", "tags": [ "nursing" ], "status": "active" }, { "id": "NURS-000009", "category": "Nursing", "subcategory": "NG Tube", "difficulty": "medium", "question": "What is the gold standard bedside test to confirm NG tube placement before feeding?", "options": [ "pH testing of aspirate (pH < 5.5)", "Air auscultation", "Water bubble check", "Visual inspection" ], "answer": 0, "explanation": "Aspirate pH < 5.5 confirms gastric placement.", "tags": [ "nursing" ], "status": "active" }, { "id": "NURS-000010", "category": "Nursing", "subcategory": "Blood Transfusion", "difficulty": "medium", "question": "How long must the nurse remain at the bedside when starting a blood transfusion?", "options": [ "First 15 minutes", "First 2 minutes", "Entire 4 hours", "First 45 minutes" ], "answer": 0, "explanation": "Acute transfusion reactions occur most frequently in the first 15 minutes.", "tags": [ "nursing" ], "status": "active" }, { "id": "NURS-000011", "category": "Nursing", "subcategory": "IV Therapy", "difficulty": "medium", "question": "An IV site is cool to touch, pale, and swollen. What complication is present?", "options": [ "Infiltration", "Phlebitis", "Thrombosis", "Air embolism" ], "answer": 0, "explanation": "Coolness and swelling signify IV infiltration.", "tags": [ "nursing" ], "status": "active" }, { "id": "NURS-000012", "category": "Nursing", "subcategory": "Assessment", "difficulty": "hard", "question": "Tapping the facial nerve anterior to the ear produces facial twitching. What is this sign?", "options": [ "Chvostek's sign (hypocalcemia)", "Trousseau's sign", "Brudzinski's sign", "Kernig's sign" ], "answer": 0, "explanation": "Chvostek's sign indicates hypocalcemia.", "tags": [ "nursing" ], "status": "active" }, { "id": "NURS-000013", "category": "Nursing", "subcategory": "ECG", "difficulty": "hard", "question": "Tall peaked T waves, prolonged PR interval, and wide QRS complexes indicate which condition?", "options": [ "Severe Hyperkalemia", "Hypocalcemia", "Hypernatremia", "Hypomagnesemia" ], "answer": 0, "explanation": "Hyperkalemia causes peaked T waves.", "tags": [ "nursing" ], "status": "active" }, { "id": "NURS-000014", "category": "Nursing", "subcategory": "Sepsis", "difficulty": "hard", "question": "In the 1-hour sepsis bundle for hypotension, what crystalloid fluid bolus is recommended?", "options": [ "30 mL/kg", "10 mL/kg", "50 mL/kg", "5 mL/kg" ], "answer": 0, "explanation": "30 mL/kg crystalloids is standard for septic hypotension.", "tags": [ "nursing" ], "status": "active" }, { "id": "NURS-000015", "category": "Nursing", "subcategory": "Pancreatitis", "difficulty": "hard", "question": "Bluish discoloration around the umbilicus in acute pancreatitis is called what?", "options": [ "Cullen's sign", "Grey Turner's sign", "Murphy's sign", "McBurney's sign" ], "answer": 0, "explanation": "Cullen's sign indicates retroperitoneal hemorrhage.", "tags": [ "nursing" ], "status": "active" }, { "id": "NURS-000016", "category": "Nursing", "subcategory": "Vital Signs", "difficulty": "easy", "question": "Which pulse site is located in the groove along the thumb side of the inner wrist?", "options": [ "Radial pulse", "Carotid pulse", "Brachial pulse", "Femoral pulse" ], "answer": 0, "explanation": "The radial artery runs along the radial bone on the thumb side.", "tags": [ "nursing" ], "status": "active" }, { "id": "NURS-000017", "category": "Nursing", "subcategory": "Thermoregulation", "difficulty": "easy", "question": "What is the medical term for an abnormally elevated body temperature or fever?", "options": [ "Pyrexia / Hyperthermia", "Hypothermia", "Eupnea", "Bradypnea" ], "answer": 0, "explanation": "Pyrexia refers to elevated body temperature / fever.", "tags": [ "nursing" ], "status": "active" }, { "id": "NURS-000018", "category": "Nursing", "subcategory": "Infection Control", "difficulty": "medium", "question": "When caring for a client with active Pulmonary Tuberculosis, what type of transmission precaution is required?", "options": [ "Airborne Precautions (with negative pressure room & N95)", "Contact Precautions", "Droplet Precautions", "Standard Precautions only" ], "answer": 0, "explanation": "Mycobacterium tuberculosis particles remain suspended in air, requiring airborne isolation.", "tags": [ "nursing" ], "status": "active" }, { "id": "NURS-000019", "category": "Nursing", "subcategory": "Fluids", "difficulty": "medium", "question": "Which laboratory finding is the most sensitive indicator of acute changes in nutritional protein status?", "options": [ "Prealbumin level", "Serum Albumin", "Total Protein", "Hemoglobin A1c" ], "answer": 0, "explanation": "Prealbumin has a short half-life of 2 days, reflecting acute nutritional status.", "tags": [ "nursing" ], "status": "active" }, { "id": "NURS-000020", "category": "Nursing", "subcategory": "Emergency", "difficulty": "hard", "question": "A client with a tracheostomy suddenly experiences acute respiratory distress. The nurse cannot pass a suction catheter. What is the immediate action?", "options": [ "Remove the inner cannula and reattempt suctioning or change the tube", "Deflate the tracheostomy cuff immediately", "Administer 100% O2 via nasal cannula", "Call for a STAT chest X-ray" ], "answer": 0, "explanation": "An obstructed inner cannula must be removed immediately to clear the airway.", "tags": [ "nursing" ], "status": "active" }, { "id": "NURS-000021", "category": "Nursing", "subcategory": "Infection Control", "difficulty": "easy", "question": "Which standard precautions measure is required for handling soiled hospital linen?", "options": [ "Wear clean gloves and avoid holding soiled linen against uniform", "Sterile gloves and gown",