d output", "Confidentiality" ], "answer": 3, "explanation": "The correct answer is Confidentiality. It matches the defining characteristic or role described in the question.", "tags": [ "nursing" ], "status": "active" }, { "id": "NURSING-MEDIUM-023-4", "category": "Nursing", "subcategory": "Nursing", "difficulty": "medium", "question": "Which option best identifies the primary purpose or role associated with Confidentiality?", "options": [ "promote safe and lawful practice", "identify poor glucose control", "maintain sterility during invasive or sterile procedures", "protect patient privacy" ], "answer": 3, "explanation": "The correct answer is protect patient privacy. It matches the defining characteristic or role described in the question.", "tags": [ "nursing" ], "status": "active" }, { "id": "NURSING-EASY-024-1", "category": "Nursing", "subcategory": "Nursing", "difficulty": "easy", "question": "Which term is best described by the following definition: infection-prevention practices applied to patient care based on potential exposure to infectious material?", "options": [ "Isometric exercise", "Orthostatic hypotension", "Standard precautions", "Medication reconciliation" ], "answer": 2, "explanation": "The correct answer is Standard precautions. It matches the defining characteristic or role described in the question.", "tags": [ "nursing" ], "status": "active" }, { "id": "NURSING-MEDIUM-024-2", "category": "Nursing", "subcategory": "Nursing", "difficulty": "medium", "question": "Which statement best describes Standard precautions?", "options": [ "protection of private patient information from unauthorized disclosure", "temperature, pulse, respirations, blood pressure, and oxygen saturation", "infection-prevention practices applied to patient care based on potential exposure to infectious material", "safe positioning and movement principles used when lifting or transferring" ], "answer": 2, "explanation": "The correct answer is infection-prevention practices applied to patient care based on potential exposure to infectious material. It matches the defining characteristic or role described in the question.", "tags": [ "nursing" ], "status": "active" }, { "id": "NURSING-HARD-024-3", "category": "Nursing", "subcategory": "Nursing", "difficulty": "hard", "question": "A learner encounters this situation: gloves are used when contact with body fluids is anticipated. Which concept best matches it?", "options": [ "Standard precautions", "Hypoglycemia", "Pressure injury", "Hyperglycemia" ], "answer": 0, "explanation": "The correct answer is Standard precautions. It matches the defining characteristic or role described in the question.", "tags": [ "nursing" ], "status": "active" }, { "id": "NURSING-HARD-024-4", "category": "Nursing", "subcategory": "Nursing", "difficulty": "hard", "question": "Which option best identifies the primary purpose or role associated with Standard precautions?", "options": [ "support autonomous decision-making", "protect tissue by relieving pressure and managing risk factors", "guide pain-management decisions", "reduce transmission of infection" ], "answer": 3, "explanation": "The correct answer is reduce transmission of infection. It matches the defining characteristic or role described in the question.", "tags": [ "nursing" ], "status": "active" }, { "id": "NURSING-EASY-025-1", "category": "Nursing", "subcategory": "Nursing", "difficulty": "easy", "question": "Which term is best described by the following definition: accurate recording of assessments, interventions, responses, and other care information?", "options": [ "Documentation", "Therapeutic communication", "Fluid overload", "Medication reconciliation" ], "answer": 0, "explanation": "The correct answer is Documentation. It matches the defining characteristic or role described in the question.", "tags": [ "nursing" ], "status": "active" }, { "id": "NURSING-MEDIUM-025-2", "category": "Nursing", "subcategory": "Nursing", "difficulty": "medium", "question": "Which statement best describes Documentation?", "options": [ "assignment of appropriate tasks to another qualified member of the care team", "accurate recording of assessments, interventions, responses, and other care information", "localized damage to skin and underlying tissue caused by pressure or shear", "cleaning hands to remove transient microorganisms" ], "answer": 1, "explanation": "The correct answer is accurate recording of assessments, interventions, responses, and other care information. It matches the defining characteristic or role described in the question.", "tags": [ "nursing" ], "status": "active" }, { "id": "NURSING-HARD-025-3", "category": "Nursing", "subcategory": "Nursing", "difficulty": "hard", "question": "A learner encounters this situation: a nurse records a medication administration and the patient's response. Which concept best matches it?", "options": [ "Delegation", "Pressure injury", "Documentation", "Hand hygiene" ], "answer": 2, "explanation": "The correct answer is Documentation. It matches the defining characteristic or role described in the question.", "tags": [ "nursing" ], "status": "active" }, { "id": "NURSING-EASY-025-4", "category": "Nursing", "subcategory": "Nursing", "difficulty": "easy", "question": "Which option best identifies the primary purpose or role associated with Documentation?", "options": [ "protect tissue by relieving pressure and managing risk factors", "support continuity, communication, and legal accountability", "reduce strain and injury during movement", "promote safe and lawful practice" ], "answer": 1, "explanation": "The correct answer is support continuity, communication, and legal accountability. It matches the defining characteristic or role described in the question.", "tags": [ "nursing" ], "status": "active" }, { "id": "PHARM-000001", "category": "Pharmacology", "subcategory": "Analgesics", "difficulty": "easy", "question": "What emergency medication reverses opioid overdose respiratory depression?", "options": [ "Naloxone (Narcan)", "Atropine", "Epinephrine", "Flumazenil" ], "answer": 0, "explanation": "Naloxone reverses opioids.", "tags": [ "pharmacology" ], "status": "active" }, { "id": "PHARM-000002", "category": "Pharmacology", "subcategory": "Antipyretics", "difficulty": "easy", "question": "Which common analgesic carries high risk of liver toxicity in overdose?", "options": [ "Acetaminophen (Paracetamol)", "Ibuprofen", "Naproxen", "Aspirin" ], "answer": 0, "explanation": "Acetaminophen can cause acute liver failure.", "tags": [ "pharmacology" ], "status": "active" }, { "id": "PHARM-000003", "category": "Pharmacology", "subcategory": "Antibiotics", "difficulty": "easy", "question": "What common class of antibiotics includes amoxicillin and piperacillin?", "options": [ "Penicillins", "Macrolides", "Aminoglycosides", "Fluoroquinolones" ], "answer": 0, "explanation": "Amoxicillin belongs to the beta-lactam penicillin class.", "tags": [ "pharmacology" ], "status": "active" }, { "id": "PHARM-000004", "category": "Pharmacology", "subcategory": "Cardiac", "difficulty": "easy", "question": "What is sublingual Nitroglycerin primarily prescribed to relieve in cardiac clients?", "options": [ "Acute angina pectoris (chest pain)", "Severe asthma attack", "Diabetic ketoacidosis", "High fever" ], "answer": 0, "explanation": "Nitroglycerin vasodilates coronary vessels to relieve angina.", "tags": [ "pharmacology" ], "status": "active" }, { "id": "PHARM-000005", "category": "Pharmacology", "subcategory": "Cardiology", "difficulty": "medium", "question": "Which blood pressure drug class commonly causes a persistent dry cough?", "options": [ "ACE Inhibitors (e.g. Lisinopril)", "Beta Blockers", "Calcium Channel Blockers", "Diuretics" ], "answer": 0, "explanation": "ACE inhibitors increase bradykinin.", "tags": [ "pharmacology" ], "status": "active" }, { "id": "PHARM-000006", "category": "Pharmacology", "subcategory": "Anticoagulants", "difficulty": "medium", "question": "What is the specific dietary education required for clients taking Warfarin (Coumadin)?", "options": [ "Maintain a consistent daily intake of Vitamin K rich green vegetables", "Completely avoid all sodium", "Eat high potassium bananas daily", "Drink 4 liters of grapefruit juice" ], "answer": 0, "explanation": "Fluctuating Vitamin K intake alters Warfarin anticoagulation efficacy.", "tags": [ "pharmacology" ], "status": "active" }, { "id": "PHARM-000007", "category": "Pharmacology", "subcategory": "Diuretics", "difficulty": "medium", "question": "Furosemide (Lasix) is a loop diuretic that requires monitoring of which serum electrolyte to prevent cardiac arrhythmias?", "options": [ "Potassium (K+)", "Calcium (Ca2+)", "Phosphate", "Iron" ], "answer": 0, "explanation": "Loop diuretics cause renal potassium excretion and hypokalemia.", "tags": [ "pharmacology" ], "status": "active" }, { "id": "PHARM-000008", "category": "Pharmacology", "subcategory": "Respiratory", "difficulty": "medium", "question": "What classification of drug is Albuterol (Ventolin) during an acute asthma attack?", "options": [ "Short-acting beta-2 adrenergic agonist (SABA)", "Inhaled corticosteroid", "Long-acting anticholinergic", "Mast cell stabilizer" ], "answer": 0, "explanation": "Albuterol is a fast-acting bronchodilator SABA.", "tags": [ "pharmacology" ], "status": "active" }, { "id": "PHARM-000009", "category": "Pharmacology", "subcategory": "Antidotes", "difficulty": "hard", "question": "What is the specific antidote used to reverse Heparin anticoagulation?", "options": [ "Protamine Sulfate", "Vitamin K", "Naloxone", "Digibind" ], "answer": 0, "explanation": "Protamine sulfate neutralizes heparin.", "tags": [ "pharmacology" ], "status": "active" }, { "id": "PHARM-000010", "category": "Pharmacology", "subcategory": "Benzodiazepines", "difficulty": "hard", "question": "What is the specific reversal agent (antagonist) for benzodiazepine overdose (e.g. Midazolam, Lorazepam)?", "options": [ "Flumazenil", "Protamine Sulfate", "N-acetylcysteine", "Deferoxamine" ], "answer": 0, "explanation": "Flumazenil is the competitive benzodiazepine receptor antagonist.", "tags": [ "pharmacology" ], "status": "active" }, { "id": "PHARM-000011", "category": "Pharmacology", "subcategory": "Therapeutic Range", "difficulty": "hard", "question": "What is the narrow therapeutic serum range for Digoxin in heart failure management?", "options": [ "0.5 to 0.9 ng/mL (or up to 2.0 ng/mL in arrhythmias)", "5.0 to 10.0 ng/mL", "10 to 20 mcg/mL", "50 to 100 mg/dL" ], "answer": 0, "explanation": "Digoxin toxicity occurs frequently when serum levels exceed 2.0 ng/mL.", "tags": [ "pharmacology" ], "status": "active" }, { "id": "PHARM-000012", "category": "Pharmacology", "subcategory": "Cardiovascular", "difficulty": "easy", "question": "What class of medication is Metoprolol (Lopressor)?", "options": [ "Beta-blocker (beta-1 selective antagonist)", "ACE inhibitor", "Calcium channel blocker", "Alpha agonist" ], "answer": 0, "explanation": "Metoprolol is a cardioselective beta-1 adrenergic antagonist.", "tags": [ "pharmacology" ], "status": "active" }, { "id": "PHARM-000013", "category": "Pharmacology", "subcategory": "Endocrine", "difficulty": "medium", "question": "What is the rapid-acting insulin analog that has an onset of action in 10-15 minutes?", "options": [ "Insulin Lispro (Humalog) / Aspart", "Regular Insulin (Humulin R)", "NPH Insulin", "Insulin Glargine (Lantus)" ], "answer": 0, "explanation": "Lispro/Aspart are rapid-acting insulins with 10-15 min onset.", "tags": [ "pharmacology" ], "status": "active" }, { "id": "PHARM-000014", "category": "Pharmacology", "subcategory": "Toxicology", "difficulty": "hard", "question": "What is the specific antidote for Acetaminophen (Tylenol) overdose toxicity?", "options": [ "N-acetylcysteine (NAC)", "Deferoxamine", "Dimercaprol", "Pralidoxime" ], "answer": 0, "explanation": "N-acetylcysteine replenishes hepatic glutathione reserves to detoxify NAPQI.", "tags": [ "pharmacology" ], "status": "active" }, { "id": "PHARM-000015", "category": "Pharmacology", "subcategory": "GI", "difficulty": "easy", "question": "What class of medication is Omeprazole (Prilosec)?", "options": [ "Proton Pump Inhibitor (PPI)", "H2 Receptor Blocker", "Antacid", "Prokinetic" ], "answer": 0, "explanation": "Omeprazole irreversibly inhibits H+/K+ ATPase proton pumps in gastric parietal cells.", "tags": [ "pharmacology" ], "status": "active" }, { "id": "PHARM-000016", "category": "Pharmacology", "subcategory": "Psychiatry", "difficulty": "medium", "question": "What class of antidepressants includes Fluoxetine (Prozac) and Sertraline (Zoloft)?", "options": [ "Selective Serotonin Reuptake Inhibitors (SSRIs)", "Tricyclic Antidepressants (TCAs)", "Monoamine Oxidase Inhibitors (MAOIs)", "Benzodiazepines" ], "answer": 0, "explanation": "SSRIs inhibit presynaptic serotonin reuptake.", "tags": [ "pharmacology" ], "status": "active" }, { "id": "PHARM-000017", "category": "Pharmacology", "subcategory": "Cardiac", "difficulty": "hard", "question": "What is the primary mechanism of action of Amiodarone in cardiac arrhythmia management?", "options": [ "Class III Potassium Channel Blocker that prolongs action potential duration", "Class I Sodium Channel Blocker", "Pure Beta-1 Agonist", "Adenosine receptor antagonist" ], "answer": 0, "explanation": "Amiodarone is predominantly a Class III antiarrhythmic prolonging repolarization.", "tags": [ "pharmacology" ], "status": "active" }, { "id": "PHARMACOLOGY-EASY-001-1", "category": "Pharmacology", "subcategory": "Pharmacology", "difficulty": "easy", "question": "Which term is best described by the following definition: the study of what the body does to a drug?", "options": [ "Anticoagulant", "Contraindication", "Dependence", "Pharmacokinetics" ], "answer": 3, "explanation": "The correct answer is Pharmacokinetics. It matches the defining characteristic or role described in the question.", "tags": [ "pharmacology" ], "status": "active" }, { "id": "PHARMACOLOGY-MEDIUM-001-2", "category": "Pharmacology", "subcategory": "Pharmacology", "difficulty": "medium", "question": "Which statement best describes Pharmacokinetics?", "options": [ "a condition in which a medication or treatment should not be used", "a medication that reduces blood clot formation", "an unintended harmful response occurring at normal drug use", "the study of what the body does to a drug" ], "answer": 3, "explanation": "The correct answer is the study of what the body does to a drug. It matches the defining characteristic or role described in the question.", "tags": [ "pharmacology" ], "status": "active" }, { "id": "PHARMACOLOGY-HARD-001-3", "category": "Pharmacology", "subcategory": "Pharmacology", "difficulty": "hard", "question": "A learner encounters this situation: absorption, distribution, metabolism, and excretion are being considered. Which concept best matches it?", "options": [ "Anticoagulant", "Contraindication", "Pharmacokinetics", "Enteral route" ], "answer": 2, "explanation": "The correct answer is Pharmacokinetics. It matches the defining characteristic or role described in the question.", "tags": [ "pharmacology" ], "status": "active" }, { "id": "PHARMACOLOGY-EASY-001-4", "category": "Pharmacology", "subcategory": "Pharmacology", "difficulty": "easy", "question": "Which option best identifies the primary purpose or role associated with Pharmacokinetics?", "options": [ "activate receptor-mediated effects", "describe drug effects and mechanisms", "describe drug movement through the body", "reduce selected beta-adrenergic effects" ], "answer": 2, "explanation": "The correct answer is describe drug movement through the body. It matches the defining characteristic or role described in the question.", "tags": [ "pharmacology" ], "status": "active" }, { "id": "PHARMACOLOGY-EASY-002-1", "category": "Pharmacology", "subcategory": "Pharmacology", "difficulty": "easy", "question": "Which term is best described by the following definition: the study of what a drug does to the body?", "options": [ "Pharmacodynamics", "Anticoagulant", "Therapeutic index", "Antibiotic" ], "answer": 0, "explanation": "The correct answer is Pharmacodynamics. It matches the defining characteristic or role described in the question.", "tags": [ "pharmacology" ], "status": "active" }, { "id": "PHARMACOLOGY-MEDIUM-002-2", "category": "Pharmacology", "subcategory": "Pharmacology", "difficulty": "medium", "question": "Which statement best describes Pharmacodynamics?", "options": [ "drug administration that bypasses the gastrointestinal tract", "drug administration through the gastrointestinal tract", "a condition in which a medication or treatment should not be used", "the study of what a drug does to the body" ], "answer": 3, "explanation": "The correct answer is the study of what a drug does to the body. It matches the defining characteristic or role described in the question.", "tags": [ "pharmacology" ], "status": "active" }, { "id": "PHARMACOLOGY-HARD-002-3", "category": "Pharmacology", "subcategory": "Pharmacology", "difficulty": "hard", "question": "A learner encounters this situation: receptor effects and physiologic responses are being considered. Which concept best matches it?", "options": [ "Adverse drug reaction", "Enteral route", "Antibiotic", "Pharmacodynamics" ], "answer": 3, "explanation": "The correct answer is Pharmacodynamics. It matches the defining characteristic or role described in the question.", "tags": [ "pharmacology" ], "status": "active" }, { "id": "PHARMACOLOGY-MEDIUM-002-4", "category": "Pharmacology", "subcategory": "Pharmacology", "difficulty": "medium", "question": "Which option best identifies the primary purpose or role associated with Pharmacodynamics?", "options": [ "activate receptor-mediated effects", "deliver medication through the digestive system", "identify clinically important medication combinations", "describe drug effects and mechanisms" ], "answer": 3, "explanation": "The correct answer is describe drug effects and mechanisms. It matches the defining characteristic or role described in the question.", "tags": [ "pharmacology" ], "status": "active" }, { "id": "PHARMACOLOGY-EASY-003-1", "category": "Pharmacology", "subcategory": "Pharmacology", "difficulty": "easy", "question": "Which term is best described by the following definition: the time required for a drug concentration to decrease by half?", "options": [ "Intramuscular route", "Half-life", "Anticoagulant", "Subcutaneous route" ], "answer": 1, "explanation": "The correct answer is Half-life. It matches the defining characteristic or role described in the question.", "tags": [ "pharmacology" ], "status": "active" }, { "id": "PHARMACOLOGY-MEDIUM-003-2", "category": "Pharmacology", "subcategory": "Pharmacology", "difficulty": "medium", "question": "Which statement best describes Half-life?", "options": [ "the time required for a drug concentration to decrease by half", "a substance that binds a receptor and blocks or reduces its activation", "drug administration through the gastrointestinal tract", "an initial larger dose used to reach a target concentration more rapidly" ], "answer": 0, "explanation": "The correct answer is the time required for a drug concentration to decrease by half. It matches the defining characteristic or role described in the question.", "tags": [ "pharmacology" ], "status": "active" }, { "id": "PHARMACOLOGY-HARD-003-3", "category": "Pharmacology", "subcategory": "Pharmacology", "difficulty": "hard", "question": "A learner encounters this situation: a medication concentration falls from 100 to 50 units. Which concept best matches it?", "options": [ "Diuretic", "Half-life", "Antibiotic", "Tolerance" ], "answer": 1, "explanation": "The correct answer is Half-life. It matches the defining characteristic or role described in the question.", "tags": [ "pharmacology" ], "status": "active" }, { "id": "PHARMACOLOGY-HARD-003-4", "category": "Pharmacology", "subcategory": "Pharmacology", "difficulty": "hard", "question": "Which option best identifies the primary purpose or role associated with Half-life?", "options": [ "deliver medication into muscle", "identify clinically important medication combinations", "produce a local or surface effect", "help predict drug accumulation and elimination" ], "answer": 3, "explanation": "The correct answer is help predict drug accumulation and elimination. It matches the defining characteristic or role described in the question.", "tags": [ "pharmacology" ], "status": "active" }, { "id": "PHARMACOLOGY-EASY-004-1", "category": "Pharmacology", "subcategory": "Pharmacology", "difficulty": "easy", "question": "Which term is best described by the following definition: the fraction of an administered dose that reaches systemic circulation unchanged?", "options": [ "Bioavailability", "Intramuscular route", "Tolerance", "Contraindication" ], "answer": 0, "explanation": "The correct answer is Bioavailability. It matches the defining characteristic or role described in the question.", "tags": [ "pharmacology" ], "status": "active" }, { "id": "PHARMACOLOGY-MEDIUM-004-2", "category": "Pharmacology", "subcategory": "Pharmacology", "difficulty": "medium", "question": "Which statement best describes Bioavailability?", "options": [ "a drug class that blocks beta-adrenergic receptors", "drug administration through the gastrointestinal tract", "administration into tissue beneath the skin", "the fraction of an administered dose that reaches systemic circulation unchanged" ], "answer": 3, "explanation": "The correct answer is the fraction of an administered dose that reaches systemic circulation unchanged. It matches the defining characteristic or role described in the question.", "tags": [ "pharmacology" ], "status": "active" }, { "id": "PHARMACOLOGY-HARD-004-3", "category": "Pharmacology", "subcategory": "Pharmacology", "difficulty": "hard", "question": "A learner